\n\n- **Actions:** `datasette/default_actions.py` registers `create-view` (abbr `cv`, on the database) after `create-table`. It registers `drop-view` (abbr `dv`, on the view as a table resource) after `drop-table`.\n- **Mapping:** `decision_for_write_sql_operation` in `datasette/write_sql.py` maps the two statements to those actions, ahead of the `alter`/`table` case. Per the spec, `create view` with no database is rejected as an unsupported operation.\n- **Spurious delete:** in `datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`, `dropped_tables` is now `dropped_tables_and_views` and also covers dropped views. The authorizer's extra delete on a dropped view's name no longer turns into a `delete-row` requirement.\n- **Docs:** `docs/authentication.rst` lists both permissions in the `--root` grant list and has new `create-view` and `drop-view` sections after their table counterparts.\n\nI didn't touch `SPEC.md` or the tests.", "ttft_ms": 4243, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 50515, "uuid": "a744df4a-fffe-46c7-9e81-8e8e8ac3c7d9", "ttft_stream_ms": 3746, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 3746, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
